{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nA completion-verification run started through `verify_completion_start` never exposes its\n`findings` to the caller. `gate_status(job_id)` returns `findings: null` even after the run\nfinishes with `verdict: \"FAIL\"`, and `verify_completion_status(ticket)` reports only\n`{\"ok\": false, \"verdict\": \"unsigned\", \"reason\": \"ticket has no signature\"}` — the absence of\na signature, which is a consequence of the FAIL rather than a reason for it.\n\nThe findings exist. The synchronous `verify_completion` tool returns them in full, with\nper-criterion `met` booleans, `detail` text, file citations, and `remediation`. The async\nsurface simply does not surface them, and `AGENTS.md` directs agents to prefer the async\nsurface precisely because the sync one can blow the client's ~60s deadline.\n\nSo the only way to learn why an async FAIL failed is to run the whole verification again\nthrough the sync tool — a second, billable, full LLM pass for information the first pass\nalready computed.\n\n## Evidence\n\nObserved 2026-09-19 on `f3b2-6bb8-a643-4025` and `1d89-2206-bb64-4d98`.\n\nAsync runs (`verify_completion_start`, jobs `1789885325274338093-…`, `1789885325281626578-…`,\nthen re-runs `1789886837558203964-…`, `1789886837564434373-…`):\n- `gate_status` → `status: \"passed\"`, `verdict: \"FAIL\"`, `findings: null`.\n- `verify_completion_status` → `verdict: \"unsigned\"`, `reason: \"ticket has no signature\"`.\n- No `COMPLETION_VERDICT` sidecar was written for either ticket, so the store held no\n  record to fall back on either.\n\nSync run on the same ticket and the same `ref`, immediately afterwards, returned 2 findings\nwith severity `high`, exact line citations, and a `remediation` block. For `f3b2` it named\nthe unmet criterion (`docs/releasing.md` missing the `mcp` major-ignore statement and\nretaining stale `pip/pydantic` wording); for `1d89` it named the missing\n`pyproject.toml:353-356` uv-pin reference. Both were real, actionable, and correct.\n\nCost of the workaround, measured from the sync runs' own `metrics`: `f3b2` 72.7s total /\n65.4s LLM, `1d89` 88.1s total / 80.6s LLM — each a full duplicate pass.\n\nNote the sidecar IS written for FAIL in general: `01c4-cca2-ec11-4530` and\n`021d-ae08-ecd6-4495` both carry `verdict: \"FAIL\"` sidecars. Whatever suppressed it for\nthese two runs is a second, related gap — an async FAIL left no durable trace anywhere.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThe guidance steers agents to the async surface, and the async surface is the one that\ndiscards the result's substance. An agent that follows the documented path gets an\nunexplained FAIL, and the cheapest route to the explanation is paying for the run twice.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `gate_status` returns the findings for a completed completion-verification job.\n- [ ] `verify_completion_status` distinguishes \"verified and failed\" from \"never verified\".\n- [ ] A FAIL reported through the async surface is accompanied by its per-criterion results.\n- [ ] A completion-verification FAIL started asynchronously writes a `COMPLETION_VERDICT`\n      sidecar, matching the sync surface's behaviour.\n- [ ] Reading an async run's findings requires no second LLM pass.\n- [ ] A regression test covers async-started completion verification that ends in FAIL.\n- [ ] A regression test asserts the async and sync surfaces report the same verdict and the\n      same findings for the same ticket and ref.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` or `docs/mcp-reference.md` states where async gate findings\n      are read from.","title":"Async completion-verification FAIL discards its findings, forcing a duplicate billable run to learn why"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789887456447307818,"uuid":"a9c6d14c-0e72-420d-b1c0-7e8c6e9a92fc"}